	"text.autoconfig.overhauleddamage.option.generalClientConfig.show_effect_build_up_elements.@PrefixText": "When an effect build-up is greater 0, a HUD element shows the progress until the effect is applied.",
	"text.autoconfig.overhauleddamage.option.generalClientConfig.show_effect_build_up_elements": "Effect build-ups are displayed in the HUD",

	"text.autoconfig.overhauleddamage.option.generalClientConfig.dynamic_offset_increase_x.@PrefixText": "\n\nWhen multiple effect build-ups are displayed at the same time, these values are added to every elements position offset, multiplied by the amount of elements already on screen.\nThe order is: bleeding, burn, freeze, poison, shock, stagger\n\nExample: The burn, poison and stagger elements are currently displayed\nThe burn element is at its normal position\nThe poison element is offset by 'dynamic_x_offset_increase' on the x axis and by 'dynamic_y_offset_increase' on the y axis\nThe stagger element is offset by 'dynamic_x_offset_increase' times 2 on the x axis and by 'dynamic_y_offset_increase' times 2 on the y axis",
	"text.autoconfig.overhauleddamage.option.generalClientConfig.dynamic_offset_increase_x": "Dynamic X offset increase",
	"text.autoconfig.overhauleddamage.option.generalClientConfig.dynamic_offset_increase_y": "Dynamic Y offset increase",


